# Qt and QGroundControl Coding Patterns

## Qt Includes and Dependencies
- Use `#include <QtPositioning/QGeoCoordinate>` for coordinate operations
- Include `#include <QtMath>` for mathematical functions
- Avoid direct `<algorithm>` includes - use Qt alternatives or manual implementations
- Link Qt modules in CMakeLists.txt: `Qt6::Positioning`, `Qt6::Core`

## QObject and QML Integration
- Inherit from `QObject` for classes used in QML
- Use `Q_OBJECT` macro for signal/slot support
- Add `QML_ELEMENT` for QML type registration
- Use `Q_INVOKABLE` for methods called from QML

## Signal/Slot Patterns
```cpp
// Declare signals in header
signals:
    void missionGenerationStarted();
    void missionGenerationCompleted(bool success, const QString& message);

// Connect in constructor or setup
connect(service, &MissionService::missionGenerationCompleted, 
        this, &SomeClass::onMissionCompleted);

// Emit signals
emit missionGenerationCompleted(true, "Mission generated successfully");
```

## QGeoCoordinate Operations
- Always check `isValid()` before using coordinates
- Use `QGeoCoordinate::distanceTo()` for distance calculations
- Use `QGeoCoordinate::azimuthTo()` for bearing calculations
- Set altitude with `setAltitude()` method

## Memory Management
- Use `QObject` parent-child relationships for automatic cleanup
- Pass `QObject* parent` parameter to constructors
- Let Qt handle deletion of child objects

## Error Handling
- Use `qCWarning` and `qCDebug` for logging
- Check for null pointers before dereferencing
- Return early on error conditions
- Provide meaningful error messages

## MAVLink Integration
- Use `MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT` for waypoint commands
- Use `MAV_CMD_NAV_LOITER_TIME` for loiter commands
- Use `MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT` for altitude frames
- Create `MissionItem` objects with proper parameters